WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
In England, Wales and Northern Ireland you must register the birth within 42 days, at the register office in your area. You usually need an appointment.

2
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:29.000
If the parents are not married and one goes alone, they may need proof of parentage from the other to include their details. Afterwards you can claim Child Benefit and tell your GP to register the baby.

3
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:37.700
If you want a passport from your country for the baby, ask your consulate which certificate they need.

4
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:44.900
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
